WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.110 --> 00:00:06.610
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this on Arrow
the streets were literally on fire.

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:10.679
A lot of big plot threads were resolved and
we’ve finally got some images for the finale

00:00:10.679 --> 00:00:11.679
next week.

00:00:11.679 --> 00:00:12.679
It was basically mass pandemonium.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:15.919
I’ve also got some news on the trailer for
the Flash TV Show.

00:00:15.919 --> 00:00:18.530
If you’re finding me for the first time
I do Arrow Videos every week.

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:25.120
In the next couple of weeks after the finale
I’ll start doing more Flash and DC bonus

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.120
videos.

00:00:26.120 --> 00:00:27.580
Be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:28.580
So real quick before we get started.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.030
The Flash rumor is that the trailer for that
will air during the Arrow Finale next week.

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:34.440
So you’d better watch.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:40.460
We’ll also find out when it’s going to
premiere in the fall too.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.630
Okay, back to Arrow.

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:46.989
Careful for spoilers from the episode if you
haven’t seen it yet.

00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:48.510
But here are my top 5 WTF moments.

00:00:48.510 --> 00:00:51.829
Number 5 - Oliver Has Failed This City

00:00:51.829 --> 00:00:53.149
It was a nice twist on the line.

00:00:53.149 --> 00:00:54.670
He had to say it at some point.

00:00:54.670 --> 00:00:58.380
Stephen Amell even commented in a recent interview
that he hadn’t said it on the show in a

00:00:58.380 --> 00:00:59.380
long time.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.960
It’s mostly a Season 1 list kind of thing.

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:07.000
Speaking of which, he also said in a Q&amp;A he
posted to his facebook page, that the List

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.320
would be coming back soon.

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:10.000
They’d start doing more list flashbacks
eventually.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.490
In the context of this episode he was just
talking about his failure to deal with Slade

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:14.630
when he had the chance.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:18.290
Because we don’t know what happened during
the final battle on the Amazo boat we can

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:19.290
only guess.

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:25.890
But it sounds like he was able to incapacitate
Slade when he shot the Arrow into his eye,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.710
but didn’t follow that up by chopping his
head off.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:32.360
In case you’re wondering, based on Merlyn
taking down the Super Soldier with the arrow.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:36.439
I think all you have to do to kill one is
land a sufficient head shot.

00:01:36.439 --> 00:01:38.650
But if you want to be sure, just chop their
heads off.

00:01:38.650 --> 00:01:45.770
Like you’re a Winchester killing vampires.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:47.620
Number 4 - Malcolm Merlyn Returns

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:52.080
We’ve known he was coming back for a long
time now, but his grand entrance was so very

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.950
Captain Jack that I cheered really loud at
my TV.

00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:59.350
John Barrowman has this swashbuckler pirate
charm that’s just so much fun to watch.

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:02.119
He’s playing Merlyn, a very very bad person.

00:02:02.119 --> 00:02:05.790
But did you see the smile on his face when
he said, “I’m Her Father.”

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:08.729
I think that was John Barrowman just having
some fun.

00:02:08.729 --> 00:02:11.500
He’s basically just trying to take Thea
away.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:14.500
I love that he’s still able to land some
jokes while the city is burning and a mirakuru

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:16.850
soldier is bashing him against a wall.

00:02:16.850 --> 00:02:18.550
That’s Captain Jack for you.

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.210
Thea did have that line, how are you still
alive?

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:23.540
And even though it wasn’t a reference to
Torchwood.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.110
I still kind of took it that way.

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:30.950
There was this interview he did where he revealed
the Arrow producers explained Merlyn to him

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.220
as a stable villain.

00:02:32.220 --> 00:02:33.709
As in like horse stables.

00:02:33.709 --> 00:02:36.860
Meaning they’d trot him out every once and
a while.

00:02:36.860 --> 00:02:39.130
Implying that he would never truly die.

00:02:39.130 --> 00:02:41.220
So take that with a grain of salt.

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:44.830
But there’s also rumors that Merlyn will
be the Season 3 big bad.

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.849
Also, I saw a lot of you commenting on Twitter.

00:02:47.849 --> 00:02:49.351
That gun shot Thea made was a fake out.

00:02:49.351 --> 00:02:50.351
She wasn’t shooting Merlyn.

00:02:50.351 --> 00:02:53.500
They just did that so you would wonder whether
or not she would.

00:02:53.500 --> 00:02:57.470
The mirakuru soldier probably just got up
behind Merlyn and that’s who she was shooting.

00:02:57.470 --> 00:03:01.360
Number 3 - Slade Watches Rome Burn

00:03:01.360 --> 00:03:02.980
I loved that Nero reference he made.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.890
I don’t ever think Slade would let anyone
catch him singing.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:08.560
But I bet he was singing inside his head.

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:11.660
Maybe evil tinkerbell shado was singing to
him.

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:15.310
Who else laughed when Isabel was like WTF
is Shado?!

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:18.610
Remember she did that, because it’s going
to come back in the finale.

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:22.440
Addressing the fact Slade is hallucinating
Shado.

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.110
Slade also revealed his true plan.

00:03:24.110 --> 00:03:25.180
To turn Starling City into ashes.

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.290
We’ve been debating on who this other person
is that Slade has to kill.

00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:30.500
Brother Blood even said, “The Person You
Love Most”.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:34.260
Part of me wants to think he was talking about
the city itself as a person.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.620
Just because I don’t think he would love
any of the women on the show more than the

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:38.650
others.

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:42.900
Like he loves his sister equally as much as
he loves felicity, sara and laurel.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.840
So the women cancel each other out and by
default, all you’re left with is the city.

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:53.830
So let’s go with that.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:56.680
Number 2 - Felicity Takes Down Isabel

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:00.799
Who else feels like this is building to a
Felicity VS Isabel fight in the finale?

00:04:00.799 --> 00:04:03.409
I loved that cut between scenes though.

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:08.069
Her asking Diggle where she was straight to
Felicity ramming her with the van.

00:04:08.069 --> 00:04:10.040
Interrogator Felicity to the rescue!

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:11.630
I was a little confused though.

00:04:11.630 --> 00:04:14.470
What did Felicity do to Isabel that would
make her want Felicity dead?

00:04:14.470 --> 00:04:17.829
Diggle was the one who killed her, and Oliver’s
father was the one who threw her away.

00:04:17.829 --> 00:04:21.680
So let me know why you think she wants Felicity
dead.

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:25.139
It might just be the smug way Felicity treated
her.

00:04:25.139 --> 00:04:28.349
Mirakuru has a way of turning insecure people
into psychopaths.

00:04:28.349 --> 00:04:31.770
I really love it when they give Felicity scenes
that are off type.

00:04:31.770 --> 00:04:35.830
Like normally she’s sitting at a computer,
so it’s so much more rewarding to see her

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:37.020
win a physical fight.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:39.460
Like during the Clock King episode when she
took the bullet.

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:42.949
I just hope that she doesn’t have to take
too many bullets in the finale.

00:04:42.949 --> 00:04:45.099
and my Number 1 WTF Moment.

00:04:45.099 --> 00:04:48.999
Amanda Waller Is Going To Destroy Starling
City To Save The Rest Of The Country.

00:04:48.999 --> 00:04:54.229
I actually expected those soldiers to be the
League of Assassins but facepalm, of course

00:04:54.229 --> 00:04:56.710
they wouldn’t roll in like the cavalry.

00:04:56.710 --> 00:05:01.119
It’s all ARGUS, and even though she said
she was using a drone strike to drop bombs,

00:05:01.119 --> 00:05:04.210
don’t be surprised if the Suicide Squad
shows up too.

00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:09.949
I feel like any episode she’s in becomes
kind of a backdoor Suicide Squad episode.

00:05:09.949 --> 00:05:12.759
Too bad Harley Quinn isn’t on the show yet.

00:05:12.759 --> 00:05:14.529
Streets of Fire seems like her kind of party.

00:05:14.529 --> 00:05:19.370
In the end I totally expect Team Arrow to
pull off the 11th Hour save and avert that

00:05:19.370 --> 00:05:20.550
drone strike.

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:26.779
I also think that we’ll end up with a situation
where it’s everyone but Slade versus Slade.

00:05:26.779 --> 00:05:29.490
Even Isabel looks like she’s seeing him
in a different light.

00:05:29.490 --> 00:05:35.139
I’m so hoping they let Felicity Kill her,
but I feel like she’ll need Sara’s help.

00:05:35.139 --> 00:05:38.380
There was also this really interesting thing
that Stephen Amell said about the finale.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:40.399
He was asked to describe it in 3 words.

00:05:40.399 --> 00:05:43.409
And he said, “Wait, He’s Where?”.

00:05:43.409 --> 00:05:49.319
I think he was referring to Slade and Oliver
learning that he was on the Island.

00:05:49.319 --> 00:05:53.020
Even if he’s not on the Island, it implies
that Slade will end up somewhere really unexpected

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:54.270
like the Foundry.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:57.120
But that feels a little too predictable.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.429
One last bonus moment too.

00:05:58.429 --> 00:06:00.800
Isabel Kills Brother Blood.

00:06:00.800 --> 00:06:05.189
There were a few things about this that surprised
me, mostly that it was not Laurel and that

00:06:05.189 --> 00:06:07.429
it happened in such a short time frame.

00:06:07.429 --> 00:06:10.969
The show had foreshadowed a conflict within
Team Deathstroke.

00:06:10.969 --> 00:06:13.869
Like the idea that Evil always turns on itself.

00:06:13.869 --> 00:06:16.869
But it feels like they should have waited
for the finale for Brother Blood to try and

00:06:16.869 --> 00:06:17.869
help Team Arrow out.

00:06:17.869 --> 00:06:19.439
It just feels like they rushed that part.

00:06:19.439 --> 00:06:21.879
But I guess it was just so that Roy could
be back for the entire duration of the finale.

00:06:21.879 --> 00:06:25.899
But now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment was?

00:06:25.899 --> 00:06:32.240
Felicity hitting Isabel with the car, Oliver
twisting his line on himself or Brother Blood’s

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.240
death?

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:37.009
Before I do my review I have a couple big
plot points I wanted to address that they

00:06:37.009 --> 00:06:38.509
didn’t cover in this episode.

00:06:38.509 --> 00:06:42.599
The biggest being Oliver’s Son, will that
come back in the finale?

00:06:42.599 --> 00:06:44.740
And if it doesn’t will you all be pissed?

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:47.969
I’d be disappointed, it such a huge reveal.

00:06:47.969 --> 00:06:51.979
Why would they tease it so late in the season
if it wasn’t going to become an integral

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:53.610
part of the finale?

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:56.330
Could that baby be the person Oliver loves
the most?

00:06:56.330 --> 00:06:59.860
Even though he doesn’t know about it, Slade
could just be assuming that if Oliver knew

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:01.750
the baby existed it would be his greatest
treasure?

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.789
Then there’s the League of Assassin’s.

00:07:03.789 --> 00:07:06.629
We know they’re coming back, we saw the
image of Nyssa.

00:07:06.629 --> 00:07:11.479
But when Sara explains why she came back,
she says nothing about bringing friends back

00:07:11.479 --> 00:07:12.479
with her.

00:07:12.479 --> 00:07:15.800
So either Sara doesn’t know they’re coming
or the writers just wanted it to be more of

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:16.800
a surprise.

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.800
So they cut a scene out of the episode where
it did get explained.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:18.800
That actually happens sometimes.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:19.800
Where scenes that explain things better just
get cut out because of time constraints.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:20.800
And then there’s the relationship of Team
Arrow with the Police Force.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.440
Clearly Quentin’s Lieutenant goes along
with Team Arrow helping because of the super

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:25.440
soldiers.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:28.210
But will that cooperation continue in Season
3.

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.370
Quentin is back to being a Detective and the
commissioner is dead.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:34.930
So I’m expecting everyone to get bumped
up the ladder and Quentin, now a full on Team

00:07:34.930 --> 00:07:36.639
Arrow member, will be in charge of the police.

00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:41.240
Making it a lot easier for him to cooperate
with Oliver’s missions.

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.869
Lots of big questions to answer in the next
week or two.

00:07:44.869 --> 00:07:49.129
Overall the episode was a solid A. Everything
about it was great, the Set Design was the

00:07:49.129 --> 00:07:52.330
best I’d seen all season.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:57.050
This was a huge undertaking with all the extra
debris, cars and literally setting the streets

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:58.150
on fire.

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.529
Then you have the stunt work.

00:07:59.529 --> 00:08:03.389
There were a few pauses in the action, but
essentially the episode itself was one continuous

00:08:03.389 --> 00:08:04.399
fight scene.

00:08:04.399 --> 00:08:08.699
It’s one thing to coreograph a fight between
two people in a small space, but there were

00:08:08.699 --> 00:08:11.770
multiple fights going on in scenes across
the entire episode.

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:16.259
I’d be willing to bet they spent more time
and energy on these last two episodes than

00:08:16.259 --> 00:08:18.469
on all the other episodes this season combined.

00:08:18.469 --> 00:08:20.209
And it was worth it.

00:08:20.209 --> 00:08:25.509
A lot of other similar shows are now being
judged by Arrow’s example.

00:08:25.509 --> 00:08:27.749
From the character development to the set
design to the action.

00:08:27.749 --> 00:08:28.881
Let’s talk about the acting really quick.

00:08:28.881 --> 00:08:32.260
In my opinion, from an acting standpoint,
Laurel, Oliver and Brother Blood tied for

00:08:32.260 --> 00:08:33.260
best performance.

00:08:33.260 --> 00:08:36.529
You expect Stephen Amell to be the best because
he’s the lead actor.

00:08:36.529 --> 00:08:39.009
But Kevin Alejandro really killed it for his
final scenes.

00:08:39.009 --> 00:08:50.129
I got this really twisted Batman vibe from
him.

00:08:50.129 --> 00:08:52.750
Like Batman put on his mask to face his fears.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:55.370
It think that was aactually a line from Batman
Begins.

00:08:55.370 --> 00:08:59.250
It’s just that the character is clearly
looney tunes and Oliver just has that moment

00:08:59.250 --> 00:09:02.629
where he’s like “you are fucking kidding
yourself if you think you still get to be

00:09:02.629 --> 00:09:03.639
mayor after all this”.

00:09:03.639 --> 00:09:06.680
I’m crossing my fingers about Oliver’s
Son next week, but otherwise I fully expect

00:09:06.680 --> 00:09:09.290
all remaining plot threads to be tied up.

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:14.050
I also think we’ll get a nice teaser for
Season 3.

00:09:14.050 --> 00:09:16.940
And that trailer for the Flash tv show.

00:09:16.940 --> 00:09:20.779
If there’s anything important you think
I left out of the video just write it in the

00:09:20.779 --> 00:09:21.779
comments.

00:09:21.779 --> 00:09:24.870
I’m posting my Q&amp;A video tomorrow, be sure
to subscribe to get everything.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:26.220
Here’s a direct link to it.

00:09:26.220 --> 00:09:30.250
I’ll add the annotation as soon as I post
it.

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.959
And click here to catch up on everything before
the finale.

00:09:32.959 --> 00:09:34.550
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:34.999
High Fives!

